WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.810
“Any changes today?”

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:05.720
the younger security officer, Zach, asked
as he stepped into the watchtower.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:11.190
“As if,” replied his superior, a jaded,
cynical old man who insisted on being referred

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.059
to as ‘Mr Jefferson’.

00:00:13.059 --> 00:00:17.310
“The darn thing hasn’t moved, spoken,
or done so much as stretch one of those wings

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.310
of his.”

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.070
“Another day at the office, then,” Zach
joked.

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:26.220
Through the window, the pair of them looked
at the towering figure a few kilometers away.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:32.730
SCP-001, the Gate Guardian, stood motionless,
its fiery sword in its hand, ever protecting

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:36.340
its post at the precipice between our world
and paradise.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:41.340
It had long been stationed at the entrance
of a dimensional gateway that led to what

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:46.870
was believed to be the Garden of Eden described
in the biblical Old Testament.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:51.660
Much like the security officers in the Foundation
base tasked with watching the Guardian, this

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.609
was pretty much the extent of the day’s
activities.

00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:58.190
“Hey, did you see that news about the transfer
posting?”

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:02.480
Zach asked, trying to stave off boredom with
as much conversation he could squeeze out

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.680
of his fellow officer.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:07.799
“Yeah, I saw it,” Mr Jefferson scoffed,
rolling his eyes.

00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:11.650
“What possesses someone like Robert Montauk
to come down here?”

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:15.560
“Must’ve wanted a quieter posting,”
Zach reasoned, looking out at the stillness

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:16.650
of the Gate Guardian.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:20.160
“Won’t find one any quieter than here,”
Jefferson mused.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.549
“Him showing up will be the most exciting
thing that’s happened here in a long while.”

00:01:24.549 --> 00:01:29.600
Unbeknownst to both Zach and Mr Jefferson,
Doctor Robert Montauk would only be joining

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:33.400
the team at the Gate Guardian observation
site for a short while.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:38.420
Not one of them, nor anybody else within the
Foundation, could ever guess Montauk’s true

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:43.799
intentions behind venturing there in the first
place: he wanted an audience with the Gate

00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:46.100
Guardian itself.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:50.380
Approaching the colossal, thousand-foot-tall
being, Doctor Montauk crossed the threshold

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.270
of the minimum safe distance from the Guardian.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:57.770
Given the sheer heat of its weapon, hotter
than Earth’s sun, anything within a kilometer

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:04.000
of SCP-001 was at risk of being obliterated,
vaporized into atoms if they didn’t turn

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.000
back.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:09.080
Which through a voice that immediately rang
out in Montauk’s ears, the Gate Guardian

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:12.069
commanded him to do.

00:02:12.069 --> 00:02:13.900
“LEAVE!”

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.690
its psychic message boomed.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.120
“Wait, wait!”

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.120
Doctor Montauk urged, holding up his hands
in what would have been a futile defense against

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.180
the Guardian’s sword.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:27.060
“I know what you do when people don’t
listen to your commands, but please just give

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:28.280
me a minute.”

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.970
There was a silence, SCP-001 didn’t reply.

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:35.879
There was nobody else close enough to hear
Montauk speak to it.

00:02:35.879 --> 00:02:39.400
So, he continued:
“You’re impossibly old.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.790
We know that much about you.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:46.010
And because of that, you must have seen things
that we can’t even begin to imagine, much

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:47.110
less fully comprehend.

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:52.231
But I’ve come a very long way to request
that you impart some information to me, if

00:02:52.231 --> 00:02:53.480
you can.”

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:58.310
He paused again, as if waiting for a reply
that never came; the Gate Guardian merely

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:01.630
stood in the same defensive, unwavering stance.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:03.540
“Tell me, please…

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:06.560
how much do you know about the Scarlet King?”

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:11.700
By this point in time, although the Foundation
was yet to realize, Doctor Robert Montauk

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:14.230
was slowly going insane.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:19.670
His investigations into an anomalous entity
known as the Scarlet King were gradually corrupting

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:25.170
him, as he tried relentlessly to quantify
exactly what this entity was and how great

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:27.290
of a threat it posed.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:32.420
Little did Montauk realize that, in trying
so hard to define and comprehend the being,

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:35.200
he was inadvertently fuelling its power.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:42.390
The Scarlet King was an interdimensional warmonger,
an embodiment of hatred and chaos, and Doctor

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:46.730
Montauk was slowly falling under the King’s
influence.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:51.450
Upon hearing the tiny human figure utter his
question, the immense Gate Guardian rebutted

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:58.060
with another single word psychic command,
one it had never been recorded giving before:

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:00.069
“WITNESS!”

00:04:00.069 --> 00:04:04.730
As if his increasing instability and the creeping
influence of the Scarlet King hadn’t made

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:08.470
Montauk feel back enough, he instantly felt
sick.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:14.010
There was a searing pain behind his eyes,
like he was staring directly at the sun, accompanied

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:16.709
by a nausea that made his head spin.

00:04:16.709 --> 00:04:21.570
It took a moment of enduring the horrific
sensations before he realized what was happening:

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:24.590
the Guardian was trying to show him something.

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:30.690
Rather than give any information on the Scarlet
King verbally, SCP-001 was imparting a psychic

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:32.340
vision onto Montauk.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:34.990
A memory of events long past?

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:36.530
The answers that he sought?

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:37.710
A warning?

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.510
Or perhaps all three.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:44.690
The vision showed Montauk a time so long ago
that it couldn’t ever be forgotten, for

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:48.340
there was barely anyone alive to remember
it in the first place.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:53.520
It was eons in the past, long before the comparatively
recent dawn of humanity.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:05:00.289
A time only spoken of in the Dust and Blood
tablet, an artifact of the Daevite civilization;

00:05:00.289 --> 00:05:03.759
some of the earliest worshippers of the Scarlet
King himself.

00:05:03.759 --> 00:05:08.870
And there, marching up to the entrance of
Eden, was the crimson-clad eldritch abomination

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:11.419
and a horde of horrors with him.

00:05:11.419 --> 00:05:15.800
According to the story recorded in the Dust
and Blood tablet, this would have been much

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:21.639
earlier in the life of the Scarlet King, perhaps
even before he assumed his now-infamous title.

00:05:21.639 --> 00:05:26.010
Back then, he would most likely have been
known as his original name of Khahrahk, one

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:31.200
of multiple siblings born when the Tree of
Life was planted, and thus created all life

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.350
in the multiverse.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:36.930
But, being the only one of his siblings cursed
with awareness.

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:41.620
Knowing the pain his existence brought him,
Khahrahk would inevitably set out on his lifelong

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:45.000
mission to destroy all of existence across
every dimension.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:52.020
And he started by killing his siblings, consuming
them to claim their power for himself.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:56.259
Around this time in pre-history, the being
that would one day be known as Scarlet King

00:05:56.259 --> 00:06:00.479
didn’t quite possess the power that he would
several millennia later.

00:06:00.479 --> 00:06:05.509
Although that’s not to say he was an unformidable
force of destruction, fuelled by his singular

00:06:05.509 --> 00:06:06.849
hatred for existence.

00:06:06.849 --> 00:06:12.460
His vow to destroy extended to the Tree of
Life that had caused him to be, along with

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:18.199
the tree’s Creator and all of their Creation
– in other words, everything in the multiverse,

00:06:18.199 --> 00:06:20.389
all of creation, if you will.

00:06:20.389 --> 00:06:25.730
So, what was the Scarlet King doing there
so long ago at the dimensional doorway protected

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:26.880
by the Gate Guardian?

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:33.290
Well, beyond the boundary between it and the
rest of the infinite multiverse, lay the supposed

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:34.290
Garden of Eden.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:39.310
While it’s unknown if it is, in fact, the
same Eden referred to in the Book of Genesis

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:42.470
is up for debate, especially among the Foundation.

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:47.400
But a glance at it, even through the gate,
will tell you that it certainly looks like

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.400
paradise.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:53.430
The space is filled with lush vegetation of
an astronomical size, populated by a number

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:56.460
of beings that seem to resemble the Gate Guardian
itself.

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:01.319
And there, protected by its watchful caretaker,
are two trees.

00:07:01.319 --> 00:07:05.289
One is thought to be the Tree of Knowledge,
that Eve was tricked into eating an apple

00:07:05.289 --> 00:07:07.620
from during the Book of Genesis.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:13.050
The other, however, bares an unknown type
of fruit and is widely believed to be… the

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:14.419
Tree of Life.

00:07:14.419 --> 00:07:18.500
Now, back in the modern age, there’s never
been a conclusive link between the Tree of

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:23.550
Life mentioned by the Daevites in their barbaric
civilization’s legends regarding the creation

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:24.680
of the Scarlet King.

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:29.531
But the fact that so long ago he and his most
feared generals were bearing down on the Gate

00:07:29.531 --> 00:07:34.440
Guardian’s position, defending a garden
where there was known to be a tree of that

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:35.440
description…

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:38.450
well, it all seems rather conclusive now.

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:44.159
Alongside Khahrahk were six of his seven daughters,
each one of them a fearsome abomination much

00:07:44.159 --> 00:07:46.169
like their destructive dad.

00:07:46.169 --> 00:07:51.920
As they approached, not one needed to exchange
any words with the angelic protector of Eden;

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:55.560
the Gate Guardian knew what these monsters
were here for.

00:07:55.560 --> 00:08:00.580
They would stop at nothing to pass through
his gate and uproot the Tree of Life, the

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:04.759
progenitor of all living beings in all existence.

00:08:04.759 --> 00:08:11.050
Even though it was early in Khahrahk’s career
as the rampaging interdimensional warlord,

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:16.300
he was as steadfast as ever in his goal to
annihilate every corner of creation.

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:22.389
Every dimension, every parallel plane of reality,
every single pocket of existence across infinity;

00:08:22.389 --> 00:08:28.220
they’d all come undone if he burned the
Tree of Life, pulled it out at the roots,

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:30.879
and splintered it until nothing remained.

00:08:30.879 --> 00:08:36.050
To the once and future Scarlet King that the
same Tree had led to his own tortured existence,

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:40.960
it was the source of his suffering, and it
had to be destroyed.

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:46.000
The only thing standing in his way was a figure
as colossal as Khahrahk himself, wielding

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.810
a flaming sword.

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:49.040
“LEAVE!”

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:51.980
boomed the psychic voice of the Gate Guardian.

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:57.000
It was like a doorman standing before a group
of rowdy teenagers trying to force their way

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:58.790
into a movie theatre.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:03.560
Except these rowdy teens were the Scarlet
King, his horrifying daughters, and the forces

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:06.290
he had already amassed since his creation.

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:11.170
The horde stood ready, waiting for the commands
of their king, who they thought would gladly

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:16.120
lead the charge as they marched on the Garden
of Eden to begin the destruction of existence.

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.640
But that’s not what happened.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:22.770
Usually, the Scarlet King would never shy
away from a fight, preferring to lead the

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:24.950
charge when it came to a slaughter.

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:29.700
Instead, he commanded his first daughter,
A’tivik to commence the first attack on

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:32.140
the protector who stood in their path.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:36.070
On her foul father’s word, A’tivik took
her horde and charged at the Guardian.

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:40.820
What she and her forces lacked in numerical
advantage, A’tivik more than made up for

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:46.940
in her knowledge of war, she hungered for
it, sought dominion – that was her seal,

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:47.940
after all.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:52.820
And yet, in the face of this impending onslaught,
the Gate Guardian remained still, rooted to

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:57.140
the spot it had always and would always be
standing in.

00:09:57.140 --> 00:10:01.630
A number of A’tivik’s minions burst into
flames, the very fabric of their crude forms

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:06.700
separated on a molecular level as they were
effortlessly rendered into nothingness.

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:12.080
Still, the Gate Guardian hadn’t appeared
to move an inch, had exerted no energy, despite

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:16.589
the damage it had done to A’tivik and her
forces in defense of Eden.

00:10:16.589 --> 00:10:21.560
As his first daughter screeched and howled
in despair at the decimation of her horde,

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:26.360
her children, the Scarlet King decided he
needed to better understand his opponent.

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:30.890
With the wave of a clawed crimson hand, the
King commanded his next daughter, A’ghor,

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:33.430
to send forth her own army.

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:39.060
In a tidal wave of nightmarish creatures,
A’ghor sent her horrific children into battle.

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:44.010
She possessed a far greater quantity to do
battle on her father’s behalf; perhaps A’ghor

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:46.680
even believed that was the Scarlet King’s
plan.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:51.209
With the greater number of her forces over
her sister’s, maybe she would be able to

00:10:51.209 --> 00:10:52.649
overwhelm the Guardian.

00:10:52.649 --> 00:10:56.870
But, even as her own children began to be
vaporized the closer that they got to the

00:10:56.870 --> 00:11:02.740
gate, A’ghor had no idea she was little
more than a pawn being sacrificed so that

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:07.300
Khahrahk could learn more about his imposing
angelic enemy.

00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:11.390
Another of the Scarlet King’s daughters,
a being known as A’nuht, was the next called

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:13.970
up to contribute to the unfolding battle.

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:18.000
Although, to call it a ‘battle’ undersells
just how easily the Gate Guardian seemed to

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:21.540
be eliminating the oncoming forces without
even moving.

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:26.480
While an outwardly frail seeming creature,
A’nuht’s primary strength over her sisters

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:32.290
was a proficiency in magic, her innate ability
to warp and reshape reality around her.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:37.250
It was that power that had caused her father
to be wary of her, viewing A’nuht’s abilities

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:39.430
as a threat to his leadership.

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:44.990
And so, Khahrahk had crippled her and all
her children, leaving them unable to overthrow

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:47.570
him, but still loyal to their King.

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:51.820
Obeying her father’s command, perhaps out
of the same loyalty or fear that he would

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:57.440
harm her and her children further if she disobeyed,
A’nuht unfurled her magic.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:02.800
She reshaped the world around them, making
it so that the passage of time moved much

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:03.800
slower.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:07.930
And that was what revealed to the Scarlet
King his enemy’s greatest strength in combat.

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:12.300
The Gate Guardian had so far been able to
obliterate both A’tivik and now A’ghor’s

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:16.540
forces without seeming to move, but it wasn’t
by standing still.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:21.870
It was moving, just much faster than the blink
of the Scarlet King’s multiple eyes.

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:26.070
Now that A’nuht’s magic had slowed the
passage of time, the Gate Guardian could be

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:27.810
seen doing battle.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:32.810
As A’ghor’s atrocities spilled toward
the angel to try and overwhelm it, it effortlessly

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:36.139
blocked the oncoming attacks with its sword.

00:12:36.139 --> 00:12:40.540
Everything the flaming blade connected with
instantly evaporated, bursting into atoms

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:45.600
as they were practically cleaved out of existence
by the Gate Guardian’s mighty weapon.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:50.670
Even with time slowed to a crawl, the towering,
winged protector of Eden only appeared to

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:52.630
be moving at an average speed.

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:58.270
But when time flowed normally, without A’nuht
manipulating reality, the Guardian was simply

00:12:58.270 --> 00:13:00.670
too fast to be observed.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:04.980
Resisting the urge to dive headfirst into
the fight himself, the Scarlet King knew it

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:07.930
would likely lead to his untimely demise.

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:13.180
He refused to accept that, it could not happen,
but he still had yet to amass the strength

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:15.760
he would as he continued his ascent.

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:20.279
So, while time was slowed to a crawl and the
Gate Guardian was still engaged in combat

00:13:20.279 --> 00:13:25.190
with A’ghor’s forces, he turned to another
of his remaining daughters: A’distat.

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:29.839
If the Scarlet King and his forces couldn’t
get past the Guardian, they could still try

00:13:29.839 --> 00:13:33.810
to get to the Tree of Life while its protector’s
focus was diverted.

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:39.030
A’distat unleashed a wave of pestilence,
sickness, and disease spewing from her in

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:44.220
a cloud of vapor, heading straight towards
the angelic guardian and Eden’s entrance

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:45.220
beyond.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:49.899
The Scarlet King knew this latest attack wouldn’t
phase or weaken the Gate Guardian; he hoped

00:13:49.899 --> 00:13:54.529
the foul smog would instead pass through the
gateway itself into the garden.

00:13:54.529 --> 00:13:59.690
As A’distat sent forth her power, blood
and ash soaked the landscape around them.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:04.399
All the plants outside the entrance to Eden
withered and died, shriveling and decomposing

00:14:04.399 --> 00:14:07.510
as the disgusting fog rolled towards the gate.

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:11.910
It washed over the Guardian, whose form only
seemed to glow brighter as he repelled the

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:12.940
pestilence.

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:17.230
It was as if it didn’t even need to think
about it, still focused on finishing off the

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:19.620
rest of the oncoming army.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:25.130
As its glow intensified, so did the fiery
sword that the Gate Guardian swung with ease

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.459
and finesse.

00:14:26.459 --> 00:14:32.950
Flames burst from the blade, the encroaching
fumes catching fire along with the air itself.

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:38.510
It ignited in a wave of fire, a defensive
inferno that repelled this latest attack.

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:44.329
But, for the brief few moments, while time
stayed slow, before A’nuht’s hold on reality

00:14:44.329 --> 00:14:48.399
inevitably broke, the King had sent forth
A’tellif.

00:14:48.399 --> 00:14:54.110
Of all his spawn, she was the most reserved,
keeping mostly to herself, never speaking.

00:14:54.110 --> 00:15:01.139
She and her children could change their faces
and forms, shift into anything or anyone and

00:15:01.139 --> 00:15:03.570
walk undetected through the multiverse.

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:10.040
And now, her father was employing her incredible
stealth abilities to slip behind enemy lines,

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:13.820
while the Gate Guardian was finishing off
the remaining onslaught from Khahrahk’s

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:15.130
other daughters.

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:20.390
It was as A’tellif drew near, creeping unseen
closer and closer to the entrance keeping

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:24.050
the Scarlet King out of Eden, that the Guardian
seemed to pause.

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:30.829
It slowly, ominously turned its huge head,
tilting until it was looking directly at A’tellif.

00:15:30.829 --> 00:15:35.769
If its expression could be seen, maybe the
Gate Guardian would almost be impressed that

00:15:35.769 --> 00:15:40.690
someone was almost able to sneak past it,
after all, it was a feat that no other being

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:42.759
in creation could ever hope to accomplish.

00:15:42.759 --> 00:15:48.699
But then again, with its steadfast conviction
and dedication to its protective duty, maybe

00:15:48.699 --> 00:15:51.399
it would have looked upon A’tellif with
anger.

00:15:51.399 --> 00:15:56.449
With a cleaving swing of its scorching sword,
the Gate Guardian unfurled a tidal wave of

00:15:56.449 --> 00:15:59.259
fire that engulfed everything around it.

00:15:59.259 --> 00:16:04.380
Not just A’tellif, but A’tivik, A’ghor,
and A’distat, all the King’s daughters

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:09.519
that had attacked so far, along with every
one of their own children, were instantly

00:16:09.519 --> 00:16:11.089
obliterated.

00:16:11.089 --> 00:16:16.149
They were all reduced to empty, vacant spaces
where they had once been, their atoms separated

00:16:16.149 --> 00:16:18.730
by a searing swing of the Guardian’s weapon.

00:16:18.730 --> 00:16:23.180
The devastating blow by his adversary did
little to deter the Scarlet King from his

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:24.180
mission.

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:29.350
He was still set on destroying the Tree of
Life, and no loss was too great in his pursuit

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:31.639
of destroying existence.

00:16:31.639 --> 00:16:35.980
He barely cared that four of his own daughters
had just been unmade by the Guardian.

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:41.209
A’nuht was still there, clinging on to time
as if it were a thrashing animal.

00:16:41.209 --> 00:16:45.839
The Scarlet King could simply make her restore
her fallen sisters and their forces.

00:16:45.839 --> 00:16:51.300
He had lost nothing, but had held back for
too long… and slowly drew his own weapon

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:53.170
out of thin air.

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:57.500
Wielding a sword that was as blood-soaked
as the Guardian’s was hot, the Scarlet King

00:16:57.500 --> 00:17:01.560
locked blades with the one being standing
in his way.

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:07.260
Both the ancient angelic defender and the
attack eldritch abomination were evenly matched,

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:11.870
every one of their vicious strikes against
the other met with an equally strong parry.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:18.110
A weapon of extreme, all-consuming heat blocked
swipes from a sharp, serrated edge that matched

00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:22.339
the deep red that would be forever synonymous
with Khahrahk.

00:17:22.339 --> 00:17:27.270
The force of their two swords clashing and
striking each other was so great that it rippled

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:28.929
out from their one-on-one fight.

00:17:28.929 --> 00:17:34.419
The landscape around them was flattened, wiped
clean of any remaining plant life that hadn’t

00:17:34.419 --> 00:17:38.510
already been destroyed by the forces of the
King’s daughters.

00:17:38.510 --> 00:17:43.090
Despite having acquired nowhere near the power
he would thousands of years after this fight,

00:17:43.090 --> 00:17:46.960
the Scarlet King was still a formidable force
in single combat.

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:52.570
And yet, the Gate Guardian seemed incapable
of tiring, or weakening, still standing strong

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:54.350
against the onslaught.

00:17:54.350 --> 00:17:58.669
Even after wiping multiple armies out with
its flaming sword, the Guardian was still

00:17:58.669 --> 00:18:05.090
able to hold its own against the Scarlet King,
who was furious, enraged at being so close

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:10.080
to the Tree of Life, yet unable to get past
his angelic adversary.

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:16.360
He needed to be stronger, faster, even more
ruthless than the warlord he already was.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:22.110
Despite A’nuht slowing down time, the King
and the Guardian were at a stalemate…

00:18:22.110 --> 00:18:23.110
Time.

00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:24.110
That was it.

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:26.640
The Scarlet King needed more time.

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:30.810
Withdrawing from the fight, he realized that
this was a battle that could not be won by

00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:32.940
sheer brute force alone.

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:38.590
His mission to destroy all Creation, to get
to the Tree of Life would take cunning, deception…

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:40.760
and more time.

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:45.700
If he let it, The Gate Guardian could easily
kill Khahrahk, its flaming weapon could cleave

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:50.159
him out of existence, and that would end the
King’s torment.

00:18:50.159 --> 00:18:55.070
But it wouldn’t be enough, a death would
be unsatisfying knowing that the rest of existence

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:57.550
would go on after he was gone.

00:18:57.550 --> 00:19:01.180
The Scarlet King couldn’t accept that, it
wasn’t enough.

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:06.900
So, he did the one thing nobody would expect
of him: he made a deal with the Gate Guardian.

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:12.410
It was an action still fuelled by his infinite
hatred for all existence, his yearning for

00:19:12.410 --> 00:19:13.880
total chaos.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:18.490
The Scarlet King knew that one day, an event
would arrive where the Guardian, and the other

00:19:18.490 --> 00:19:24.289
beings like it in the Garden of Eden, would
spill forth and deliver judgement on this

00:19:24.289 --> 00:19:25.289
world.

00:19:25.289 --> 00:19:29.490
And when that Rapture happened, the Tree of
Life would be undefended.

00:19:29.490 --> 00:19:34.200
The Scarlet King bartered with the Guardian,
that he would retreat for the time being,

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:38.342
so he could spend eons amassing more and more
power.

00:19:38.342 --> 00:19:43.720
Then, when the fateful day arrived, the Gate
Guardian would allow him into Eden to destroy

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:49.010
the Tree of Life, while it and its brethren
were busy conducting the Rapture.

00:19:49.010 --> 00:19:53.600
Halting their fight, the Scarlet King offered
a crimson claw to the Gate Guardian’s burning

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:54.600
hand…

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:56.880
***
Returning to reality from the intense vision,

00:19:56.880 --> 00:20:01.540
still feeling sick at what he had witnessed,
Robert Montauk looked up at the still, silent

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:02.750
form of the Gate Guardian.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:07.590
“Did you do it?” he yelled, desperate
to know more through his obsession with the

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:08.590
Scarlet King.

00:20:08.590 --> 00:20:09.740
“Did you tell him yes?

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:11.130
Did you make a deal?”

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:16.490
There was no answer from the Guardian, just
a single word that echoed through Montauk’s

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:20.290
fractured mind:
“LEAVE!”

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:26.260
